# Example 41: Two-species cross-feeding (L3 syntrophy, doc/19 §5.3)
# A sustained chemostat mutualism: the fermenter runs glucose -> acetate
# overflow (waste secretion) while the acetotroph lives on that secretion,
# so producer's waste is consumer's food.  The flow rate sets the balance
# point: at flow_rate=0.002 the pair coexists at a stable steady state
# (fermenter ~33, acetotroph ~89, glucose ~0.1 mM fed in as consumed,
# acetate ~0 consumed on the fly) - a textbook cross-feeding loop in the
# ecosystem backend (sim_runtime._run_ecosystem, apps/ecosystem.py).

#species name=fermenter substrate=glucose vmax=0.03 ks=0.2 cn_ratio=6 maintenance=0.001 secretion=acetate:0.004
#species name=acetotroph substrate=acetate vmax=0.012 ks=0.05 cn_ratio=6 maintenance=0.0015

#patch name=chemostat kind=chemostat flow_rate=0.002 anoxic=true initial.fermenter=20 initial.acetotroph=5 initial_nh4_mm=200 substrate.glucose.initial=50 substrate.glucose.bulk=50 substrate.acetate.initial=0 substrate.acetate.bulk=0

#config backend=ecosystem

#sim kind=ecosystem ticks=4320 seed=7 fast_forward=false sample_every=432
#sim output=tick,chemostat:fermenter,chemostat:acetotroph,chemostat:glucose,chemostat:acetate,chemostat:co2
